<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isabella of Angoulême</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1188–1246</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isabella of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/angouleme">Angoulême</a>, heiress of the county of Angoulême, married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-king-of-england">King John</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> in 1200, which provoked the Lusignans and helped bring on the loss of Normandy. After John's death she returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and married Hugh X of Lusignan, count of La <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marche">Marche</a>, joining his failed revolt against Louis IX in 1242.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isabella-of-angouleme.jpg" alt="Isabella of Angoulême" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: UAltmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IsabelledAngouleme.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
